Only add the vendored Skia to the include path when building it from source.

The sdist vendors a full Skia checkout, so with BUILD_SKIA_FROM_SOURCE=0 the
vendored headers still come first on the include path and shadow the ones
belonging to the Skia we actually link against. That is silently wrong: the two
trees can disagree about the defines in SkUserConfig.h and about which APIs are
compiled into the library at all (e.g. SK_HIDE_PATH_EDIT_METHODS), which shows up
as undefined symbols or, worse, as an ABI mismatch at runtime.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -340,7 +340,10 @@
 skia_dir = os.path.join(skia_builder_dir, "skia")
 skia_src_dir = os.path.join(skia_dir, "src")  # allow access to internals

-include_dirs = [skia_dir, skia_src_dir, *pkg_config_op.include_dirs]
+if BUILD_SKIA_FROM_SOURCE:
+    include_dirs = [skia_dir, skia_src_dir, *pkg_config_op.include_dirs]
+else:
+    include_dirs = [*pkg_config_op.include_dirs]

 extra_compile_args = {
     "": [
